{"availability":"available","full":"shlokchorge/Fine-Tuning-QWEN2vl","name":"Fine-Tuning-QWEN2vl","description":"Fine-tuned Qwen2-VL-7B for LaTeX OCR using LoRA and Unsloth on the LaTeX OCR dataset. Built augmentation pipeline (rotation, noise, contrast jitter), ran LoRA rank sweep (r=8/16/32), and evaluated across CER, Token F1, BLEU-4, and Exact Match. Deployed as a Gradio Space with live metric computation.","category":"Education","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":33,"forks":1,"created":"2026-02-13T02:06:00Z","updated":"2026-06-25T06:39:11Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/shlokchorge2929/visiontex","topics":["computer-vision","deep-learning","fine-tuning","gradio","latex","lora","ocr","qwen2","transformers","unsloth"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/shlokchorge2929/visiontex","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:31:24.631Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:31:24.631Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:31:24.631Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T17:13:33.514Z","stars":32,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-08T22:31:24.631Z","stars":33,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["VisionTeX is a mathematical expression recognition system built by fine-tuning Qwen2-VL-7B-Instruct on the LaTeX OCR dataset using Unsloth and LoRA. Given an image of a mathematical expression, the model produces the corresponding LaTeX source code. The project covers the full pipeline — training, evaluation, a Gradio demo, and a merged model checkpoint for direct deployment.","Checkpoint trained for 500 steps on T4 (partial run). Full-epoch checkpoint in progress — metrics will be updated.","The base model, Qwen2-VL-7B, has seven billion parameters. Even in float16, the weights alone occupy around 14 GB of GPU memory. Before generating a single token the model must load those weights, encode the image through the vision encoder, and then run an autoregressive decode loop — each token requires a full forward pass through all layers."],"features":["A100 40 GB or 80 GB — the recommended card for this model class. Memory bandwidth is roughly 3x the T4, and bfloat16 is supported natively, which speeds up both training and inference.","RTX 4090 (24 GB) — a practical consumer alternative. Not as fast as an A100 for training but significantly faster than a T4 for inference.","H100 — the fastest available option, most relevant if you want to run full-epoch training with larger batch sizes."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/shlokchorge/Fine-Tuning-QWEN2vl/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8570ec2617a9b5cc2ebfa5344ea500afd4cc7e1f1cda5cad74d11f10c51c7ea8","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T17:13:33.669Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:13:33.669Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"VisionTeX is a mathematical expression recognition system built by fine-tuning Qwen2-VL-7B-Instruct on the LaTeX OCR dataset using Unsloth and LoRA. Given an image of a mathematical expression, the model produces the corresponding LaTeX source code. The project covers the full pipeline — training, evaluation, a Gradio demo, and a merged model checkpoint for direct deployment.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/shlokchorge/Fine-Tuning-QWEN2vl/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"8570ec2617a9b5cc2ebfa5344ea500afd4cc7e1f1cda5cad74d11f10c51c7ea8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/shlokchorge/Fine-Tuning-QWEN2vl/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T17:13:33.669Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-06-25T06:39:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/shlokchorge/Fine-Tuning-QWEN2vl/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T17:13:33.670Z","hash":"8570ec2617a9b5cc2ebfa5344ea500afd4cc7e1f1cda5cad74d11f10c51c7ea8","originalBytes":7822,"storedBytes":7822,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["model","adapter","training","run","base","checkpoint","full","inference","latex","lora","merge","weights","a100","app.py","demo","im